ng represents the level curves of $f(x,y)=2x+y?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421492 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ca25fed3-89e3-5069-b0f1-d69395195a30" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421492 #edb/ref 1074 "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nNotice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider level curves for any value of $c.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ 2x+y & =c \\\\ y & =-2x+c.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of lines with slope of $-2.$ Therefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/ff/ff1117065d7475786dd6c45f71f14d78b32cb3273123ced1adf5a67b750dacdd.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421493 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186421496 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421493 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "21b773b4-bd95-5150-b031-ba25c0bc0edb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421493 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125014 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421494 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186421497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421494 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "35ace902-fd84-5342-8e5b-38d0d8036933" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421494 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186262943 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421495 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6ed691e2-551c-53fd-a582-b1d42ed0b3f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421495 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186387992 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421496 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186421494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421496 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d24eeca1-18a8-58f3-b314-b346d5df791c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421496 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186338937 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421497 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186421495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421497 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d88cafd9-c924-5a6c-a387-1de1666c815e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186421497 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186421492 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
